# V3 Heston–Merton period notebooks — option-implied calibration

When editing files under `V3-Models_result/heston merton notebook/`:

- Euler MC must use the current \(v_t\) for the stock return over \([t,t+\Delta t]\), then update \(v_{t+\Delta t}\). Do not look ahead. Leave the Fourier NLS calibrator and LSM algorithm unchanged.
- **Do not** use Method A for \((\kappa,\theta,\xi,\rho,v_0)\) (no AR(1) RV, no realized-variance \(\theta\), no residual \(\xi\)).
- Calibrate \((\kappa,\theta,\xi,\rho,v_0)\) from listed call prices using the Bates characteristic function, with jump parameters held from the 3σ return threshold.
- True rolling-window calibration: re-fit from the current lookback of option quotes; use those params for the next Monte Carlo segment.
- Do **not** mix Method B (advanced folder) into this folder.
- See `V3-Models_result/heston merton notebook/ROLLING_CALIBRATION.md`.
